# cw-tune-tuner: the same CW page as cw-tune-default with the "Tuner" button
# pressed, and a synthetic tone so the active block is drawn (issue #122).
#
# Same route (KEY pages -> "(CW 1:2)"); the difference is scenario_settle pressing
# the page's "Tuner" button (index 2), which runs the user's path
# button_action_cb -> controls_toggle_cw_tuner -> cfg.cw_tune (src/buttons.cpp,
# src/controls.cpp). The parameter no longer gates the widget (that was the cause
# of #122), but the button still exists and still has to work: the fixture
# codifies that it flips the parameter and that its label follows.
#
# The active block is drawn by the real cw_tune_set_freq() with a synthetic 8 Hz
# tone: on the radio the tone comes from the DSP (src/cw.cpp, update_peak_freq),
# which the bank has no way to feed. scenario_settle codifies the parameter, the
# button label and the widget's visibility.

name cw-tune-tuner
screen cw-tune-tuner

theme Redshift
seed 20

frequency_hz 7030000
tx_frequency_hz 7030000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
